{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"✨Fuddles✨","id":"403783497564684291","is_bot":0,"username":"fuddlescottage"},"author_id":"403783497564684291","channel_id":"850780876140183553","content":"They chose a character angle that is a trigger and added a little sexual harassment. I want a player to have fun but there is absolutely a line you don't cross and it was crossed.","created_at":"2021-07-30T15:02:05.279000Z","edited_at":"2021-07-30T15:02:33.959000Z","id":"870682671045541989","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"hekiryuu","id":"237577351532249110","is_bot":0,"username":"hekiryuu"},"author_id":"237577351532249110","channel_id":"850780876140183553","content":"I dont like the idea of telling people how to roleplay... In many cases I feel our server rules are a bit too restrictive, but they do generally make for safer play space so I support them especially in this format.\n\nBut when you start bordering on turning a mental disorder into a gimmick, it puts me in a place where I want to say something.  And even if Liz doesn't have DID, it feels like its imitating the general feel of how people role play it (as if it was a joke).  Its kinda like, I wouldn't let someone play a character with tourettes.  So I was already trying to formulate how best to talk to them, but now its even more compounded by their... gross... push into what I consider a type of roleplay that requires consent.\n\nAs you know fuddles.. I was always making sure I didn't cross a line with you last year for this reason.","created_at":"2021-07-30T15:02:43.708000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"870682832228462612","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"hekiryuu","id":"237577351532249110","is_bot":0,"username":"hekiryuu"},"author_id":"237577351532249110","channel_id":"850780876140183553","content":"thank you.... thats the concept i was struggling to get to... characters are very personal to people, and that level of overt pushiness became a type of sexual harassment that went beyond the characters, and was not welcome roleplay.  Generally before saying something like that, it should be discussed oocly","created_at":"2021-07-30T15:04:56.413000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"870683388833595402","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"✨Fuddles✨","id":"403783497564684291","is_bot":0,"username":"fuddlescottage"},"author_id":"403783497564684291","channel_id":"850780876140183553","content":"And I appreciated that and that is another thing us mods talked about. Was having a rule added so that player know they have to ask for consent before starting any relationship with another character. And that when is any doubt ask for consent first.","created_at":"2021-07-30T15:07:05.973000Z","edited_at":"2021-07-30T15:07:38.858000Z","id":"870683932247609394","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"mazie","id":"366565198284324868","is_bot":0,"username":"damnzam"},"author_id":"366565198284324868","channel_id":"850780876140183553","content":"i felt that whole thing too with Willow and Irynx especially since i know i made it known very often that me — and my characters — are not the type for romance. \n\nand while i hoped they'd respect that, it still felt like toeing the boundaries i had set just to add some unrequited love drama without really discussing it with me","created_at":"2021-07-30T15:07:24.527000Z","edited_at":"2021-07-30T15:10:22.569000Z","id":"870684010068721745","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
